      "title": "k12: Fix leak of duplicated srcdsc hash entries.",
      "message": "k12: Fix leak of duplicated srcdsc hash entries.\n\nCreate the src_by_id hash with a value_destroy_func, which takes care of\nfreeing the values for us, including in the case where the same key appeared\nmultiple times in the capture file -- where previously the old value would leak\nwhen the new value was added to the hash.\n\nThis makes src_by_name hash entirely redundant -- its sole use was freeing the\nsrcdsc records -- so delete it.\n\n\n(cherry picked from commit f0f6cfc72f532634e0d8bbdcb8977718cf4aa0a7)\n\nCo-authored-by: Darius Davis <darius-wireshark@free-range.com.au>",
      "author_name": "Guy Harris",
      "author_email": "gharris@sonic.net",
      "authored_date": "2025-09-11T02:07:38.000+00:00",
